</reasoning>

<solution>
```python
def identify_sofa(d, n, m, sofas, cnts):
    for i, (x1, y1, x2, y2) in enumerate(sofas):
        l, r, t, b = 0, 0, 0, 0
        for j, (x3, y3, x4, y4) in enumerate(sofas):
            if i != j:
                if x3 == x1 or y3 == y1:
                    l += 1
                if x4 == x2 or y4 == y2:
                    r += 1
                if x3 == x1 and y3 == y2:
                    t += 1
                if x4 == x2 and y4 == y2:
                    b += 1
        if l <= cnts[0] and r <= cnts[1] and t <= cnts[2] and b <= cnts[3]:
            return i + 1
    return -1
```
</solution>


