I’ll use Python’s built-in zip function to iterate through the array in pairs, which makes it easier to keep track of the last minimum and the last distance.
</reasoning>

<solution>
```python
def min_distance(arr):
    last_min = None
    last_distance = 0
    for i, j in zip(arr, arr[1:]):
        if i == j:
            if last_min is None:
                last_min = i
            else:
                distance = j - last_min
                if distance < last_distance:
                    last_distance = distance
                last_min = j
    return last_distance
```
</solution>


