Second, we need to consider the edge cases. If there is only one row in the class, then the teacher always asks children from this row. So, we should handle this case separately.

Third, we need to consider the order of asking pupils. We can use a dictionary to keep track of the number of questions for each pupil, and then find the maximum and minimum values.

