2. If the array is unimodal, print "YES". Otherwise, print "NO".
</reasoning>

<solution>
```python
def is_unimodal(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    if n < 3:
        return True

    prev = arr[0]
    for i in range(1, n):
        if arr[i] == prev:
            return False
        elif arr[i] > prev:
            prev = arr[i]
        else:
            return False

    return True

def main():
    n = int(input())
    arr = list(map(int, input().split()))
    if is_unimodal(arr):
        print("YES")
    else:
        print("NO")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
```
</solution>


